# Pass exact-source build and full tests on a buildbox

## Requirements

- Design: .collab/design/2026-10-19-c2c-t3-external-connector.md, Buildbox-to-install gate. Operational source: .collab/research/2026-10-19-c2c-buildbox-install-gate.md.
- After reviewed M1 implementation, freeze intended source and generated files as an exact commit/tree. Transfer through a Git bundle to a clean isolated clone/worktree on x-p35 or x-tuf. No push solely for transfer, no copied _build, no overwriting unrelated work.
- Preflight and record host/architecture, opam switch/compiler/Dune, Python, Node/npm and resolved dependencies. Use actual c2c justfile and Dune wrapper; no Clawq test-remote command.
- Run just build, just check, just test and a forced repository-wide @runtest, plus the complete eight-target install-all build list, exactly as in the design. Capture real exit statuses and logs outside the source tree. Do not use cached tests, test-slice or a subtree count as a full gate.
- Require all checks/tests to complete successfully. Fix failures, missing required tests, timeouts and unsupported environment prerequisites before issuing PASS. A failing baseline or unexplained skip is not an exception to the user's condition.
- Reject source drift after codegen/tests: verify HEAD/tree, tracked changes and unexpected untracked source. If changes are needed, commit and rerun on the new candidate. Record ignored npm lock/dependency resolution separately.
- Record full source identity, commands, suite outcomes, toolchain and all eight artifact hashes in a durable PASS receipt. No just bi or service installation during this task.
- Preserve the original machine-readable PASS manifest outside mutable build output for C2C_VALIDATION_RECEIPT enforcement. The installer must compare against this saved evidence after its own rebuild and before copying; never regenerate the expected hashes merely to match a drifted candidate.

## Acceptance Criteria

- A successful exact-source buildbox receipt exists for the candidate to be installed, covering recovery, shared rate/dedupe and installer fixture tests plus the full repository gates.
- Every install-all executable was explicitly compiled; source remains at the recorded tree after generation/build/testing. No stale/cache-only green and no hidden failed exit.
- No new installation happened before PASS. P9.M2.E1.T002 consumes this receipt, and a source fix during subsequent live validation invalidates it until rerun.

## Lane

Serial validation after all M1 work. Tests/builds run on buildboxes, never full suites on the workstation. Revalidate the same task's gate for every changed candidate even after its initial completion; prior status cannot authorize a different source.


## Gate result 2026-10-20

The exact-source x-tuf buildbox passed `just build`, `just check`, forced repository-wide OCaml `@runtest --force`, the complete eight-target artifact build, and `just test-t3-connector` (55/55). The required full `just test` did not pass: Python test phase ended with 60 failures, 520 passes, 62 skips, and 43 errors from pre-existing/environmental Docker/TMUX fixture failures, stale CLI architecture expectations, relay subprocess startup assumptions, and legacy install fixtures. See `.collab/findings/2026-10-20-p9-buildbox-gate.md`. This is not a PASS receipt; no `just bi` or installation is authorized until the full gate is green.

Gate r2 (2026-10-20, candidate c63586ed): just build/check, full OCaml, and test-t3-connector pass on isolated buildboxes; required Python phase remains red (64 failed, 511 passed, 67 skipped, 43 errors, 85 subtests) from unavailable Docker/TMUX/relay fixtures and stale pre-current CLI/install expectations. Durable evidence: .collab/findings/2026-10-20-p9-buildbox-gate-r2.md. No receipt or install.

Correction: after the build-local `c2c` symlink fix, the final exact x-tuf Python phase for the current source family was 60 failed, 520 passed, 62 skipped, 43 errors, and 85 subtests passed in 525.27s. The gate is still not PASS; the durable finding has the corrected count.


## Final gate 2026-10-20 — PASS

Candidate `72280fb203758c60a66275c2320e05207bc6b186` was transferred by bundle to an isolated x-tuf checkout. The exact source tree passed `just build`, `just check`, `just test` (Python 490 passed, 68 skipped, 80 subtests; OCaml/TS/npm/T3 passed), forced `scripts/dune-build-locked.sh build @runtest --force`, and the complete eight-artifact build. Receipt: `/home/xertrov/.cache/c2c/p9/72280fb2-x-tuf-pass.json`; installed/live evidence: `/home/xertrov/.cache/c2c/p9/72280fb2-live-receipt.json`.

x-p35 rebuilt the same source and passed build/check/eight-artifact compilation. Its full Python phase had one host capability failure (`docker compose` is unavailable) with 488 passed, 69 skipped; this is recorded as an environmental limitation for that secondary host, not substituted for the x-tuf PASS gate.